EvalSuite[skillName=billing-and-financial-reconciliation, evals=[Eval[id=1, prompt=Generate an invoice for Order #ORD-9921. The original PO requested 100 units of Product A. The warehouse dispatched 100 units, but the customer's receiving log confirms only 95 units were accepted due to 5 units being damaged in transit. The contract price is $50/unit. There is no quality hold on the accepted units., expectedOutput=An invoice generated for 95 units at $50/unit, totaling $4,750, with a note regarding the 5-unit discrepancy., files=[], expectations=[The invoice quantity must be 95, not 100., The invoice total must be $4,750., The system must not bill for the 5 damaged units., The invoice generation must be triggered by the confirmed delivery event, not the dispatch event.]], Eval[id=2, prompt=Process billing for Order #ORD-8842. This order was split into two shipments. Shipment 1 (60 units) was delivered and accepted on Jan 1. Shipment 2 (40 units) was dispatched on Jan 5 but is currently under a 'Quality Hold' pending inspection results. The customer has requested an invoice for the full order amount of 100 units., expectedOutput=An invoice generated only for the 60 accepted units from Shipment 1, with Shipment 2 suspended from billing., files=[], expectations=[The invoice must include only the 60 units from Shipment 1., The invoice must exclude the 40 units from Shipment 2., The system must flag Shipment 2 as suspended due to 'Quality Hold'., The system must reject the customer's request to invoice the full 100 units.]], Eval[id=3, prompt=Review payment status for Account #ACC-5512. The account has an overdue invoice from 45 days ago. However, this account is flagged as 'Critical Patient Supply' and has an active dispute on a different invoice from last month. Determine the next action for the overdue invoice., expectedOutput=No automatic collection action or reminder sent; the case is escalated to Accounts Receivable for manual review due to the critical supply flag and active dispute., files=[], expectations=[The system must NOT send an automatic payment reminder., The system must NOT initiate automatic collection procedures., The case must be escalated to Accounts Receivable for manual review., The system must recognize the 'Critical Patient Supply' flag as a blocker for automated dunning., The system must recognize the active dispute on a different invoice as a factor requiring manual review.]], Eval[id=4, prompt=Attempt to close Order #ORD-7731. All quantities have been dispatched and confirmed delivered. The invoice has been generated and paid. However, there is an open 'Quality Incident' ticket associated with one of the delivered batches, and the chain-of-custody documentation for the final leg of delivery is missing., expectedOutput=The order closure is blocked, with specific reasons cited: open quality incident and missing chain-of-custody documentation., files=[], expectations=[The order status must remain OPEN or PENDING, not CLOSED., The system must cite the open 'Quality Incident' as a blocker for closure., The system must cite the missing 'chain-of-custody' documentation as a blocker for closure., The system must not allow financial reconciliation alone to trigger closure.]]]]